New blocker F7: the adv 7 pin does not count or strip a mid-line or multi-line disable
comment. directiveKindsOfFile (scripts/__tests__/oxc-toolchain-gates.test.ts:981-1005 at
the audited HEAD) counts only a whole-line block comment (WHOLE_LINE_DISABLE_RE, line
901) and a "//"-trailing comment. stripDisableComments (lines 907-913) strips only those
two forms. oxlint 1.93.0 honors both evading forms: the live controls of adv 9 (committed
after my HEAD, at 490af011) pass, because a seeded mid-line "const keep = 1; /*
eslint-disable */" and a multi-line form both hide no-unused-vars with exit 0. I re-ran
the strip logic of the audited HEAD directly (node -e): both stripped copies keep the
disable comment, so the sweep's temp copy stays suppressed and the hidden rule never
surfaces. A pinned carrier can therefore hide a new live finding behind either form while
adv 7 passes (A4: the guard can pass while its claim is false). No current carrier uses
either form (the in-code claim at lines 898-899 holds; my kinds recount matched all 49
entries), so the recorded phase state stays true, but the guard that PM option B relies
on is evadable. The committed failing guard adv 9 proves the gap after my HEAD. Route to
Green: widen WHOLE_LINE_DISABLE_RE, directiveKindsOfFile, and stripDisableComments to
count and strip mid-line and multi-line block comments, so adv 9 passes.

